course: dictionary
lesson: 4903
title: Illustration: pictures and examples
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An illustration is a picture or drawing that helps explain a text or makes it more interesting. «The book had colour illustrations on every page.» The pictures show you what the characters look like and what is happening in the story.
explain: An illustration can also be an example that helps explain an idea. «By way of illustration» means "as an example". So if someone says, «Here is an illustration of what I mean», they are about to show you one example.
explain: Use the words around the word to decide which meaning fits. In a story, it is a picture. In science, a labelled illustration can show how something works. Then check by swapping in your meaning: "the picture helps explain" should still make sense.
fact: An illustration is a picture or drawing in a book, magazine or poster.
fact: An illustration can also be an example that helps explain an idea.
fact: An illustrator is the person who draws illustrations.
fact: «Pictures are for illustration» means the picture may not show exactly what you get.
fact: Adverts often show a product at its very best, sometimes with special effects, so the real thing may do less than the picture.
exercise: «The book had colour illustrations on every page.» What are the illustrations? | *Pictures or drawings that help explain the story | Long lists of words to learn | Stickers to peel off the cover | Pieces of cloth
exercise: Maya's toy box says «pictures are for illustration». What is this warning her about? | The toy is free with the box | The toy is made of paper | The picture on the box is the real toy | *The real toy may do less than the picture shows
exercise: Mr Khan says, «This diagram is a good illustration of how the heart pumps blood.» What does illustration mean here? | A loud noise made by the heart | *An example or picture that explains an idea | A test for the class | A story about a doctor
test: «The illustrator drew a dragon on every page.» Who draws illustrations? | A librarian | A referee | *An illustrator | A postman
test: «By way of illustration, she gave three examples.» What does by way of illustration mean? | In a hurry | In a whisper | *As an example | As a joke
exam: «The labelled illustration showed the parts of a flower clearly.» What does labelled illustration most likely mean? | A very long story | *A drawing with names on its parts | A flower in a vase | A loud sound
